      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hey everyone! We are looking for more info on this issue to provide a fix.\n\nFor that reason, we have enabled a custom debug beta on Steam. You can enable it with the password `audiotest1234`, the branch is called `a-test`.\n\nEDIT: The branch has a new build now which should in theory fix the issue! Please report if you can hear voices now. If you still cannot, perform the steps below and drop your logs please!\n\nTest instructions:\n\n- Opt in to the `a-test` branch and launch VRChat in Desktop mode.\n\n- Visit this world: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_26501c5c-ca19-47b0-aeca-8a8f69b519c7/info\n\n- You can click the red spheres to turn them green, and they should all play audio.\n\n- If you are affected by this bug, I suspect you will only hear one of them. Two will turn green, but remain silent. Make sure you have your World volume up.\n\n- Close VRChat and submit your logs here! They may be large, so you can host them on pastebin, gist.github.com, or similar, and link them here. Here is a help page showing you where to find your logs: https://help.vrchat.com/hc/en-us/articles/9521522810899-Where-do-I-find-my-Output-Logs-and-Crash-Dumps\n\n- Lastly don't forget to switch off of `a-test` again.\n\nThanks in advance for your help! We really do want to fix this issue, but it is hard without a solid repro.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
